---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";

const snapshot = [
  { label: "Client / Program", value: "T. Rowe Price" },
  { label: "Role", value: "Sr. UX/UI Consultant" },
  { label: "Product", value: "Web / Mobile" },
  { label: "Industry", value: "Financial Services / Fintech" },
  { label: "Scale", value: "5-person cross-functional team" },
];

const methodology = [
  "Frame - Align and define",
  "Discover - Research and empathize",
  "Structure - Information architecture",
  "Ideate - Explore concepts",
  "Interact - Optimize flows",
  "Design - Visual and systems",
  "Validate - Test and reduce risk",
  "Launch - Build and QA",
  "Improve - Measure and learn",
];

const deliverables = [
  "Bite-sized insight cards with cross-indexing",
  "Intuitive data drill-down models",
  "Mobile-first investment dashboards",
  "Complex data visualization patterns",
  "Responsive platform design",
  "Portfolio exposure visualization",
  "Interactive financial charts and graphs",
  "Decision-support tools",
];

const methods = [
  "Axure RP",
  "Sketch",
  "InVision",
  "Wireframing",
  "Interactive prototyping",
  "Usability testing",
  "Data visualization",
  "Responsive web and mobile design",
];

const outcomes = [
  "Supported more informed investment decision-making",
  "Made complex financial data easier to scan and interpret",
  "Improved clarity around portfolio exposure and risk information",
  "Reduced friction in moving from high-level insights to detailed analytics",
  "Strengthened cross-device access through responsive design",
  "Supported a more guided investor analysis experience",
];

const workedWell = [
  "Bite-sized insight cards communicated critical data points quickly and clearly.",
  "A mobile-first approach supported a seamless experience across devices.",
  "Interactive charts and graphs improved engagement with complex financial data.",
];

const improvements = [
  "Future versions could explore more advanced personalization for investor insights.",
  "Additional performance optimization would further improve responsiveness for data-heavy views.",
];

const takeaways = [
  "Combining qualitative insight with quantitative data creates a more complete understanding of investor needs.",
  "Continuous user feedback is essential when designing complex financial platforms.",
  "Strong financial UX requires balancing simplicity with analytical depth.",
];
---

<MainLayout
  title="High-End Investor Platform | Jorge Obando"
  description="T. Rowe Price case study by Jorge Obando, covering investor platform design, data visualization, mobile and responsive UX, drill-down models, insight cards, and decision-support tools."
  ogImage="/images/t-rowe-price-investor-platform-case-study.png"
>
  <section class="case-study-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">T. Rowe Price</p>
        <h1>High-End Investor Platform</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          A web and mobile investor platform designed to make complex financial data
          easier to understand through clearer dashboards, insight cards, drill-down
          models, visualizations, and decision-support tools.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="hero-image">
        <img
          src="/images/t-rowe-price-investor-platform-case-study.png"
          alt="T. Rowe Price high-end investor platform interface screenshot"
        />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="snapshot-grid" aria-label="Case study snapshot">
      {snapshot.map((item) => (
        <article class="snapshot-card">
          <p class="snapshot-label">{item.label}</p>
          <p class="snapshot-value">{item.value}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        T. Rowe Price faced a challenge common in high-end investment experiences:
        users needed access to deep financial information, but dense data and complex
        interfaces could make it difficult to identify the right insights quickly.
      </p>
      <p>
        As Sr. UX/UI Consultant, Jorge supported the design of a web and mobile
        investor platform focused on clearer data visualization, more intuitive
        drill-down patterns, bite-sized insight cards, and decision-support tools.
      </p>
      <p>
        T. Rowe Price needed to help high-end investors navigate and interpret large
        volumes of complex financial data. The objective was to create a clearer,
        more usable web and mobile platform that could surface meaningful insights,
        support decision-making, and balance simplified data presentation with the
        analytical depth sophisticated investors require.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>The real problem</h2>
      <p>
        High-end investors often need to navigate large volumes of complex financial
        data to make informed investment decisions.
      </p>
      <p>
        The strategic challenge was creating clarity and usability within dense,
        technical information while preserving the depth necessary for analysis.
      </p>
      <p>
        The experience needed to help users move from high-level portfolio insights
        to detailed analytics without feeling overwhelmed.
      </p>
      <p>
        The core design problem was balancing simplicity and depth: reducing cognitive
        load while still supporting sophisticated financial decision-making.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Role and leadership</h2>
      <p>
        As Sr. UX/UI Consultant, Jorge worked with a cross-functional team that
        included data analysts, designers, and software engineers.
      </p>
      <p>
        His responsibilities included UX strategy, interaction design, visual design,
        stakeholder collaboration, ideation facilitation, and translating user needs
        into actionable design requirements.
      </p>
      <p>
        The role required aligning investment user needs with business goals while
        helping shape interaction models for data-rich financial experiences.
      </p>
      <p>
        The work involved a 5-person cross-functional team. Collaboration was
        primarily on-site, supporting close coordination between data analysts,
        designers, engineers, and stakeholders throughout research, prototyping,
        testing, and refinement.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Methodology</h2>
      <p>
        The work followed a research-led, structure-first design process with
        continuous validation. The approach emphasized research over opinion,
        structure before surface, and continuous usability validation.
      </p>
      <div class="cards-grid three-up">
        {methodology.map((item) => (
          <article class="info-card compact-card">
            <p>{item}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Key deliverables</h2>
      <div class="outcomes-card">
        <ul>
          {deliverables.map((item) => (
            <li>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Design process</h2>
      <div class="cards-grid one-up">
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Research and discovery</h3>
          <p>
            The research approach combined qualitative and quantitative methods.
          </p>
          <p>
            The team conducted in-depth interviews with high-end investors to
            understand pain points, behavior patterns, and expectations around
            financial data access.
          </p>
          <p>
            Surveys and broader insight gathering helped identify the need for concise
            data summaries, robust filtering, and drill-down capabilities.
          </p>
          <p>
            Users expressed a preference for visual representations that could help
            them move quickly from summary-level information to deeper analysis.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Information architecture</h3>
          <p>
            The information architecture strategy focused on creating a user-centered
            framework that prioritized accessibility, intuitive navigation, and
            progressive disclosure.
          </p>
          <p>
            The team structured content around investor needs, defined clearer paths
            for data exploration, and created hierarchical models that allowed users
            to drill down from high-level insights to detailed analytics.
          </p>
          <p>
            This structure gave users more control over the complexity of information
            while preserving analytical depth.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Prototyping and testing</h3>
          <p>
            The team used an iterative prototyping process, starting with low-fidelity
            wireframes and progressing to high-fidelity interactive prototypes.
          </p>
          <p>
            Usability testing sessions with representative users helped evaluate
            functionality, clarity, and ease of use.
          </p>
          <p>
            Feedback from testing informed refinements before implementation,
            grounding the design in observed user behavior.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Iterations and refinements</h3>
          <p>
            The design process went through multiple iterations based on user testing
            feedback.
          </p>
          <p>
            Users highlighted the need for more interactive elements, clearer visual
            representations, and stronger decision-support tools.
          </p>
          <p>
            These insights led to refinements in data visualization, dashboard
            hierarchy, insight-card behavior, and drill-down interactions.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Technologies and methods</h2>
      <div class="tag-list" aria-label="Technologies and methods">
        {methods.map((item) => (
          <span>{item}</span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Outcomes</h2>
      <p>
        The design work supported T. Rowe Price's goals around improving investor
        clarity, strengthening cross-device access, and making complex financial data
        easier to interpret.
      </p>
      <p>
        By focusing on digestible visualizations, insight cards, drill-down models,
        and decision-support patterns, the platform helped investors move through
        complex information with greater confidence and control.
      </p>
      <div class="outcomes-card">
        <ul>
          {outcomes.map((item) => (
            <li>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Reflection</h2>
      <div class="cards-grid one-up">
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>What worked well</h3>
          <ul>
            {workedWell.map((item) => (
              <li>{item}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Areas for improvement</h3>
          <ul>
            {improvements.map((item) => (
              <li>{item}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
          <ul>
            {takeaways.map((item) => (
              <li>{item}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Why this matters</h2>
      <p>
        Investor platforms must help users move from dense financial information to
        clear, trustworthy insight without stripping away analytical depth. Strong
        financial UX gives users a path from summary to detail while keeping complex
        data understandable and actionable.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Related Thinking</h2>
      <section class="article-links" aria-label="Related thinking and next navigation">
        <a href="/thinking/measuring-what-matters">
          Why measuring outcomes - not outputs - changes execution
        </a>
        <a href="/thinking/designing-through-change">
          Designing systems that evolve through change
        </a>
        <a href="/case-studies">
          Return to all case studies
        </a>
      </section>
    </section>
  </section>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .case-study-page {
    padding: 2.5rem 0 5rem;
  }

  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(320px, 0.9fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: end;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .hero-copy {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #a33a3a;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4vw, 4.15rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .lead {
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #555;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .hero-image {
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--divider);
    border-radius: 18px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .hero-image img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 280px;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .snapshot-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .snapshot-card,
  .info-card,
  .outcomes-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--divider);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .snapshot-card {
    padding: 1.2rem;
  }

  .snapshot-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #777;
  }

  .snapshot-value {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #222;
  }

  .content-section {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 2.2vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .content-section p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #444;
    line-height: 1.8;
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .cards-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .cards-grid.three-up {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .cards-grid.one-up {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .info-card {
    padding: 1.4rem;
  }

  .compact-card {
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
  }

  .info-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .info-card p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .info-card p:last-child,
  .compact-card p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .info-card ul,
  .outcomes-card ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .info-card li,
  .outcomes-card li {
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #444;
  }

  .info-card li:last-child,
  .outcomes-card li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .outcomes-card {
    padding: 1.35rem 1.4rem;
  }

  .tag-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .tag-list span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--divider);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
    color: #444;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .article-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .article-links a {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .snapshot-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .cards-grid.three-up {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .case-study-page {
      padding: 1.5rem 0 4rem;
    }

    .snapshot-grid,
    .cards-grid.three-up {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: 1.02rem;
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .hero-image img {
      min-height: 220px;
    }

    .article-links {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.35rem;
    }
  }
</style>
